---
// Observation, forecast, and local-action resources answer different questions.
---

<div class="decision-pipeline">
  <div class="pipeline-header">
    <p class="answer">
      A hurricane is not a single point on a map. Making safe, timely decisions requires matching the question you have to the official source designed to answer it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="pipeline-grid">
    <!-- Step 1: Observe -->
    <article class="pipeline-card step-observe">
      <div class="card-badge-row">
        <span class="step-num">Step 1</span>
        <span class="source-tag"><i class="fa-solid fa-satellite" aria-hidden="true"></i> Radar &amp; Satellite</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card-title-group">
        <span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i></span>
        <h3>Observe What Is Happening Now</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="card-question"><strong>Answers:</strong> Where is rain actively falling right now, and what does the storm's cloud structure look like?</p>

      <div class="card-body">
        <ul class="guidance-list">
          <li><strong>Radar:</strong> Shows observed precipitation echoes where radar coverage is available. Check the frame time; observations are not a forecast of the next six hours.</li>
          <li><strong>Satellite (GOES-East):</strong> Shows cloud structure; infrared and water-vapor products add cloud-top and atmospheric-moisture context, not surface wind measurements.</li>
          <li class="warning-point"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i> <em>Neither radar nor satellite loops establish a future landfall or your local flood risk.</em></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card-footer">
        <a class="action-btn" href="/radar/">
          <span>Open Interactive Radar</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Step 2: Understand Track -->
    <article class="pipeline-card step-track">
      <div class="card-badge-row">
        <span class="step-num">Step 2</span>
        <span class="source-tag"><i class="fa-solid fa-hurricane" aria-hidden="true"></i> National Hurricane Center</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card-title-group">
        <span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-route"></i></span>
        <h3>Understand Track &amp; Uncertainty</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="card-question"><strong>Answers:</strong> Where is the center forecast to move over the next 1 to 5 days? What do NHC advisories say about intensity?</p>

      <div class="card-body">
        <ul class="guidance-list">
          <li><strong>Official Cone:</strong> Uses circles sized to contain two-thirds of NHC center-track forecast errors from the previous five years. It is not a storm-specific impact probability.</li>
          <li><strong>Cone vs. Impact:</strong> Dangerous winds, flooding, and storm surge frequently extend <em>far outside</em> the cone.</li>
          <li class="warning-point"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i> <em>Never focus solely on the center line. Hazards extend across hundreds of miles.</em></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card-footer">
        <a class="action-btn" href="/hurricane-tracker/live/">
          <span>Open Live Storm Tracker</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Step 3: Act on Local Alerts -->
    <article class="pipeline-card step-act">
      <div class="card-badge-row">
        <span class="step-num">Step 3</span>
        <span class="source-tag"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved" aria-hidden="true"></i> Local NWS &amp; Emergency Mgmt</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card-title-group">
        <span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-bullhorn"></i></span>
        <h3>Act on Official Local Alerts</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="card-question"><strong>Answers:</strong> Is my neighborhood at risk of storm surge, wind damage, or mandatory evacuation?</p>

      <div class="card-body">
        <ul class="guidance-list">
          <li><strong>Official Alerts:</strong> Read NHC and local NWS watches and warnings for the hazard, affected area, timing, and protective action. Begin preparing before a warning.</li>
          <li><strong>Evacuation Orders:</strong> Check the responsible local authority's current instructions. Zone names vary; orders may cover surge areas, flood-prone neighborhoods, or mobile homes, not just a wind category.</li>
          <li class="warning-point highlight"><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i> <strong>Follow evacuation orders promptly. Plan earlier for medical or transport needs; do not wait for an order to respond to immediate danger.</strong></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card-footer">
        <a class="action-btn action-btn-primary" href="/alerts/">
          <span>Check Local Alerts</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
        <a class="sub-link" href="/tools/evacuation-decision-helper/">Use Evacuation Helper &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <!-- Bottom Takeaway Banner -->
  <div class="pipeline-takeaway">
    <div class="takeaway-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-compass"></i>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway-text">
      <strong>Core HurricaneHub Principle:</strong>
      <span>Maps provide context, not a household safety determination. Follow official instructions, prepare early, and respond to immediate danger. HurricaneHub does not issue forecasts or evacuation orders.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="pipeline-sources">Official references: <a href="https://www.weather.gov/jetstream/remote/intro">NWS remote sensing</a>, <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/aboutcone.shtml">NHC cone definition</a>, and <a href="https://www.ready.gov/evacuation">Ready.gov evacuation planning</a>.</p>

  <!-- Expandable Diagram for Visual Learners -->
  <details class="pipeline-diagram-toggle">
    <summary>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-image" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span>View illustrative concept diagram (Visual Infographic)</span>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down toggle-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </summary>
    <div class="diagram-wrap">
      <picture>
        <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="/images/guides/hurricane-decision-path-mobile.png" width="750" height="800" />
        <img src="/images/guides/hurricane-decision-path-desktop.png" alt="Conceptual infographic showing the relationship between radar observation, NHC forecast track, and local NWS warnings" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </picture>
      <p class="diagram-caption">Illustrative map only, not a current forecast. Maps provide context; verify current NHC advisories, local NWS alerts, and official emergency instructions before acting.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>

<style>
  .decision-pipeline {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .pipeline-header {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .pipeline-header .answer {
    max-width: 820px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .pipeline-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  .pipeline-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 24px 20px;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: var(--soft-shadow);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .pipeline-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    border-color: #0e6f8f;
  }

  .card-badge-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .step-num {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding: 3px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #e2e8f0;
    color: #334155;
  }
  .source-tag {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--muted);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
  }

  .card-title-group {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .card-icon {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 38px;
    height: 38px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .pipeline-card h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* Specific step accent colors */
  .step-observe .card-icon {
    background: rgba(14, 111, 143, 0.12);
    color: #0e6f8f;
  }
  .step-observe .step-num {
    background: rgba(14, 111, 143, 0.15);
    color: #0e6f8f;
  }

  .step-track .card-icon {
    background: rgba(32, 56, 77, 0.12);
    color: #20384d;
  }
  .step-track .step-num {
    background: rgba(32, 56, 77, 0.15);
    color: #20384d;
  }

  .step-act {
    border-color: rgba(193, 68, 46, 0.35);
  }
  .step-act .card-icon {
    background: rgba(193, 68, 46, 0.14);
    color: #c1442e;
  }
  .step-act .step-num {
    background: rgba(193, 68, 46, 0.16);
    color: #c1442e;
  }

  .card-question {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--line);
  }
  .card-question strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .card-body {
    flex-grow: 1;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .guidance-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .guidance-list li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .warning-point {
    list-style: none;
    margin-left: -18px;
    margin-top: 12px !important;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: #f8fafc;
    border-left: 3px solid #64748b;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #475569;
  }
  .warning-point.highlight {
    background: #fef2f2;
    border-left-color: #dc2626;
    color: #991b1b;
  }

  .card-footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: auto;
  }
  .action-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .action-btn:hover {
    background: #e2e8f0;
    color: #0e6f8f;
  }
  .action-btn-primary {
    background: #c1442e;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .action-btn-primary:hover {
    background: #a83623;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .sub-link {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #0e6f8f;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4px 0;
  }
  .sub-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* Takeaway banner */
  .pipeline-takeaway {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    background: rgba(14, 111, 143, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(14, 111, 143, 0.25);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .takeaway-icon {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: #0e6f8f;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .takeaway-text {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .takeaway-text strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-right: 6px;
  }

  /* Optional toggle diagram */
  .pipeline-diagram-toggle {
    margin-top: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--panel);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .pipeline-diagram-toggle summary {
    padding: 12px 18px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    background: var(--surface);
    user-select: none;
  }
  .pipeline-diagram-toggle summary:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .diagram-wrap {
    padding: 16px;
    background: var(--panel);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .diagram-wrap img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .diagram-caption {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .pipeline-sources {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .pipeline-sources a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .toggle-chevron {
    margin-left: auto;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  details[open] .toggle-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }
  .decision-pipeline a:focus-visible,
  .pipeline-diagram-toggle summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }
  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .card-icon,
  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .step-num {
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .sub-link,
  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .takeaway-icon {
    color: #7dd3fc;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .pipeline-card {
      transition: none;
    }
    .pipeline-card:hover {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .pipeline-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .pipeline-card {
      padding: 20px 16px;
    }
    .pipeline-takeaway {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
